   "stem": {
      "text": "A particle moves along the x-axis with velocity \\( v(t) = 6 t^{2} + 4 t + 5 \\) meters per second, where t is measured in seconds, for \\( t \\ge 0 \\). At time t = 3 the position of the particle is \\( x(3) = 3 \\) meters. Find the position of the particle at time t = 1.",
      "command_verb": "find"
   },
   "answer_key": {
      "form": "symbolic",
      "mathjson": -75,
      "units": "meters"
   },
   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "Position changes by the integral of velocity, so \\( x(1) = x(3) + \\int_{3}^{1} v(t)\\,dt \\).",
         "rule_named": "position from velocity by accumulation"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "An antiderivative of v is \\( 2 t^{3} + 2 t^{2} + 5 t \\), so \\( \\int_{3}^{1} v(t)\\,dt = \\left[2 t^{3} + 2 t^{2} + 5 t\\right]_{3}^{1} = -78 \\).",
         "mathjson": -78,
         "rule_named": "fundamental theorem of calculus"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "Add the known position: \\( x(1) = x(3) + \\int_{3}^{1} v(t)\\,dt = 3 - 78 = -75 \\) meters.",
         "mathjson": -75,
         "rule_named": "add the initial position"
      }
   ],
